# The pogo folio touchpad must NOT be paired with the tablet-mode switch:
# the kernel pins SW_TABLET_MODE on (auto-rotation is gated in userspace),
# and libinput suspends INTERNAL touchpads while a tablet-mode switch is
# active — which would kill the folio touchpad permanently. External
# touchpads are exempt from the tablet-mode suspension (and DWT pairing
# with the folio keyboard works via the libinput quirk file shipped in the
# same package).
#
# ID_INTEGRATION is the property libinput >= 1.32 reads first; the
# ID_INPUT_TOUCHPAD_INTEGRATION fallback is what 1.31 and older used. This
# touchpad hangs off the pogo serial controller, so systemd's
# 65-integration.rules tags it "internal" from ID_BUS=platform and
# 70-touchpad.rules copies that back — set both, or a libinput upgrade
# silently suspends the touchpad again (seen on the Arch/Omarchy image).
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="OnePlus Pad 3 Touchpad", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHPAD}=="1", ENV{ID_INTEGRATION}="external", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHPAD_INTEGRATION}="external"
